    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** leading the way at a 77.46, buoyed by a favorable matchup against Rocker and a dynamic platoon advantage that boosts his offensive upside. Close behind is **James Wood**, whose 72.41 score reflects his elite 0.415 xwOBA and the massive statistical bump provided by his leadoff position against Ure\u00f1a. **Brice Turang** and **Trevor Story** also represent strong starts, both exceeding the 67-point mark; **Brice Turang** thrives in the #2 hole with a 12% boost from Singer\u2019s SP skill profile, while **Trevor Story** benefits from an exploitable 4.58 xERA from Dobnak, positioning him as a primary engine for our counting stats.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Isaac Paredes**, who finished just shy of the lineup with a 38.96 score, failing to clear our 40.0 floor. While his #2 batting order position kept him in contention, his 19% downgrade against Seymour\u2019s skill set and a significant platoon disadvantage proved too heavy a burden for the optimizer to overcome. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Austin Riley**, who barely justifies his spot at 42.69; he faces a tough 3.25 xERA arm in Mayza and suffers from a notable \"Elite Catcher\" defensive penalty. If we were chasing a higher floor, he would be the first candidate for rotation.\n\nBeyond the bench, proceed with caution regarding **Griffin Conine** (40.08) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (52.77). **Griffin Conine** is barely clinging to a start against the formidable Glasnow, whose 3.02 xERA drastically suppresses the expected output, leaving **Griffin Conine** as a high-risk play. Similarly, **Vinnie Pasquantino** is hindered by a 15% platoon penalty against Suarez. We are currently navigating these matchups while keeping **Jose Caballero**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Max Muncy**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Zach McKinstry**, and **Edwin Arroyo** on standby, ensuring we maintain depth as **Tyler Soderstrom** remains sidelined on the IL.",
